== cross-pool absorption: harvest(A) reads whole-vault balances (L11209-L11213) ==
  R1 push of B's rewards=False: harvest(A) -> 50000000000000000000 aFXS, harvest(B) -> 50000000000000000000 aFXS; pending alice=50000000000000000000 bob=50000000000000000000
  R1 push of B's rewards=True: harvest(A) -> 100000000000000000000 aFXS, harvest(B) -> 0 aFXS; pending alice=100000000000000000000 bob=0

== FXS/cvxFXS type aliasing in _claim (L17816-L17830) ==
  alice pending aFXS = 100000000000000000000; vault cells = {'aFXS@vault': 100000000000000000000}
  claim as 0x3432..(FXS): REVERT('transfer amount exceeds balance [0x3432..(FXS) of vault]')  <- vault holds no FXS
  claim as 0xFEEf..(cvxFXS): REVERT('transfer amount exceeds balance [0x3432..(FXS) of vault]')  <- vault holds no FXS
  claim as USDC: REVERT('transfer amount exceeds balance [0x3432..(FXS) of vault]')  <- vault holds no FXS
  claim as ETH: REVERT('transfer amount exceeds balance [0x3432..(FXS) of vault]')  <- vault holds no FXS
  -- now some FXS (pool C's unharvested extra reward) sits in the vault (R1: getReward(vault) on C) --
  vault cells = {'0x3432..(FXS)@vault': 150000000000000000000, 'aFXS@vault': 100000000000000000000}
  alice claim as FXS: received 120000000000000000000 FXS (= redeemed cvxFXS amount 120000000000000000000); vault cells now {'0x3432..(FXS)@vault': 30000000000000000000, '0xFEEf..(cvxFXS)@vault': 120000000000000000000}
  harvest(C) afterwards -> 25000000000000000000 aFXS for carol (should be 125000000000000000000 without the alias); carol pending=25000000000000000000
  -- ETH branch (L17825-L17828) sends `_amount` (aFXS shares) to msg.sender, not `_amountOut` to recipient --
  claim as ETH with no ETH in vault: REVERT('transfer amount exceeds balance [ETH of vault]')
  claim as ETH with 200e18 wei in vault: returns _amountOut=120000000000000000; msg.sender(alice) got 100000000000000000000 wei; recipient(alice_rx) got 0; vault ETH left 100120000000000000000

